            "n_events": 25,
            "result_text": "Done. The function uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit concurrency and `asyncio.gather()` to run all tasks. When you hit Ctrl+C:\n\n1. **KeyboardInterrupt** interrupts the gather call\n2. All pending tasks are automatically cancelled by asyncio\n3. Each task's **cleanup code** (try/finally blocks, context managers) runs during cancellation\n4. The interrupt propagates naturally\n\nYou can import it as `from run import run_tasks` and use it like:\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def my_task():\n    try:\n        await asyncio.sleep(10)\n    finally:\n        print(\"Cleanup!\")\n\nasyncio.run(run_tasks([my_task, my_task], max_concurrent=2))\n```"
        }
